# vbscript: Implement IActiveScript::InterruptScriptThread.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12655 state=merged
# A running script can now be aborted through `IActiveScript::InterruptScriptThread`, from the script thread or from any other thread:

```c
IActiveScript_InterruptScriptThread(script, SCRIPTTHREADID_BASE, &ei, SCRIPTINTERRUPT_RAISEEXCEPTION);
```

The error from the passed `EXCEPINFO` is raised at the next statement, can't be handled with `On Error Resume Next` and is reported through `OnScriptError`. As on native, the engine stays interrupted until the script state is set again: calls into the script fail with `E_FAIL` and new script text is queued instead of run.

The call only succeeds while a script is running, and the flags are ignored, like native does.

Known difference: when the interrupt hits the end of a procedure, the error is located at its last statement instead of its `End` line (marked `todo_wine`).
